      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/chaetostoma-joropo-l445-2/",
      "html": "<p>It originates from creeks in the catchment area of the Rio Meta in Colombia.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/chaetostoma-joropo-l445-2/",
      "html": "<p>It does not need to be kept as warm as many other L-numbers, 23-27°C are just right.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/chaetostoma-joropo-l445-2/",
      "html": "<p>Juveniles may arrive with such a strong metallic-green shimmer that the species-typical spots are not visible. This phenomenon is also known from Corydoras catfish. In the aquarium this green shimmer disappears after a while.</p>"
    }
